    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `telephoneDisplay` (the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans), keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nThree files touched, each change small and low-complexity:\n\n1. **`util/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive `format(String)` helper: `'+'` + country code + space + national digits grouped in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). Country-code split mirrors `E164` (`+1` is one digit, otherwise two). Null/non-E.164 input passes through unchanged. New class, so zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto` delegating to the new helper. The method itself stays trivial (CC 1, one changed line).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field.\n\nI deliberately put the logic in a fresh helper and mapped it via a one-line expression rather than adding a derived getter to the large `Owner` entity or growing `E164`, keeping WMC_other \u2248 1 for the new work and each edited function simple. Both the new acceptance test (`coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
